WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
A new 0.8 billion on-device model doubles agentic benchmark scores while keeping all data private. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 231. Time series forecasting, chat GPT business agents, then things to try. Tether AI research put bot-sci on hugging face as a fine-tune of Qwen 3.50.8B for function calling and agentic workflows. It supports tools for web search, travel, commerce, device control, files, calendar,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.620
and messaging, aimed at low-to-medium difficulty tasks.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:42.140
Tool use results for its size are state-of-the-art, lifting BFCL version 4 from 23.4 to 44.0,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:49.460
AC bench from 30.1 to 58.7, and Tau bench from 23.2 to 51.5.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.140
The model makes no third-party API calls, avoiding the cost of frontier cloud models, intended

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.500
And it used guidance points it at personal assistance and edge deployments and says it

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.560
is not suited for high stakes decisions.

00:01:03.488 --> 00:01:09.048
Time Omni-01, an archive paper describes, couples' time series foundation models with

00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:13.168
large language models or LLMs for joint reasoning and forecasting.

00:01:13.848 --> 00:01:20.148
The architecture packs each series into a compressed encoding the LLM can read, then routes the LLMs

00:01:20.148 --> 00:01:23.408
reasoning back into the time series model to produce the forecast.

00:01:23.408 --> 00:01:30.588
training used the new MMTR data set of more than 500,000 multi-modal samples across 12 domains.

00:01:31.308 --> 00:01:36.748
The system beats both standalone LLMs and time series models on understanding and forecasting,

00:01:37.288 --> 00:01:39.908
and those gains transfer to three open benchmarks.

00:01:41.045 --> 00:01:46.665
Converting a hybrid attention model to pure bite-level inference is the claim of one bite, one token.

00:01:47.345 --> 00:01:52.765
The 27 billion parameter starting point shrinks its vocabulary to 384 entries.

00:01:52.765 --> 00:02:01.925
Continued training used 4.77 GB of self-generated dialogue and encyclopedia data for 178.6 hours

00:02:01.925 --> 00:02:04.045
on 8H-200 GPUs.

00:02:04.445 --> 00:02:10.845
The resulting model matches the original on Math 500, Human Eval Plus, and MMLU Pro,

00:02:11.405 --> 00:02:16.605
while improving character-level tasks at the cost of 3-5 times lower token throughput.

00:02:17.546 --> 00:02:22.886
Target Android phones get task-specific small-language models searched and quantized by mobile

00:02:22.886 --> 00:02:29.026
AI factory. The agentic system tries base models and quantizations against real device measurements

00:02:29.026 --> 00:02:34.606
and rolls back any change that hurts accuracy. Across ten tasks and four phones,

00:02:34.886 --> 00:02:41.006
the resulting on-device models beat five-shot frontier models on five tasks and match them on three

00:02:41.006 --> 00:02:47.966
more using 19 times less GPU time than exhaustive search. Camoon delivers a morphine segmenter

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:52.506
that works at the morphological level rather than the word level to avoid compounding

00:02:52.506 --> 00:03:00.186
ambiguity. The 1 million parameter model posts a boundary F1 of 0.992 for tie. It was trained

00:03:00.186 --> 00:03:05.346
on guidelines with near-perfect human agreement and annotation scales through an LLM plus

00:03:05.346 --> 00:03:10.946
human correction. Downstream models trained on its morpheme output match or exceed word-level

00:03:10.946 --> 00:03:16.246
baselines on part of speech tagging, named entity recognition and sentiment classification.

00:03:16.246 --> 00:03:22.033
Reducing interference during LLM knowledge editing is the job of capacity allocation,

00:03:22.473 --> 00:03:26.013
which uses L1 regularization on target hidden states.

00:03:26.353 --> 00:03:30.673
The method prunes unused pieces of each knowledge vector before the parameter edit,

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:36.553
and experiments across multiple LLMs and benchmarks show fewer side effects on unrelated knowledge

00:03:36.553 --> 00:03:38.093
while preserving edit success.

00:03:39.141 --> 00:03:41.761
Biomedical agents are the setting for biomem,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.561
a training-free framework of hybrid memory retrieval and utilization.

00:03:45.561 --> 00:03:52.981
It improves evidence accessibility and task-aware utilization across five memory approaches and four LLMs.

00:03:53.461 --> 00:03:59.921
The result is an 8.6% relative gain on biomedical question answering and conversational memory benchmarks,

00:04:00.361 --> 00:04:05.116
and conversational answer errors fall by 24.9%.

00:04:05.116 --> 00:04:12.596
Synapse control selects and times advice for agent experience reuse using a classifier instead of a generative model for diagnosis.

00:04:12.596 --> 00:04:20.776
across 1,308 attempts on app world and web shop, it records 29.8% more successes than the base agent,

00:04:21.216 --> 00:04:27.436
replacing 4,987 generative diagnosis calls and cutting auxiliary control time in half.

00:04:28.374 --> 00:04:33.934
Rendering documents as images is how optical rag feeds retrieval augmented generation or rag,

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:39.274
using encoder-bridged retrieval and query-driven distillation without cross-modal training.

00:04:39.274 --> 00:04:46.934
Visual tokens distilled down to 16 injected tokens. On LongBench V2, Bamboo, and Lugel V2,

00:04:47.114 --> 00:04:53.314
it records the best compression-aware accuracy, lifting a 7 billion quen 2.5 instruct backbone

00:04:53.314 --> 00:05:00.500
by 5.17 points on LongBench V2. Polly Route is a code-mixed benchmark for type decision routing

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:07.600
with 13 system baselines. It holds 322 native messages, 156 code-mixed items,

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.600
programs, and optional training rows across 12 languages and 9 scripts.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:18.740
The best fine-tune reaches 96.6% accuracy, and TFI-DF with logistic regression hits

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:21.226
91.9%.

00:05:21.226 --> 00:05:26.406
Storing reusable procedural logic in editable programs rather than natural language documents

00:05:26.406 --> 00:05:29.686
is the design of program-aided patchable skill evolution.

00:05:30.346 --> 00:05:35.306
Past splits trajectory-derived experience into executable programs that can be patched

00:05:35.306 --> 00:05:37.026
without rewriting descriptive text,

00:05:37.366 --> 00:05:40.346
and it improves success rates by more than 2.8%

00:05:40.346 --> 00:05:42.486
over prior skill evolution baselines

00:05:42.846 --> 00:05:44.766
with greater evolutionary stability

00:05:44.766 --> 00:05:46.266
across models and benchmarks.

00:05:47.372 --> 00:05:50.392
Open AI put businesses and chat GPT into beta

00:05:50.392 --> 00:05:52.672
with business agents and engagement insights.

00:05:53.372 --> 00:05:55.512
Eligible businesses can claim their profile,

00:05:56.052 --> 00:05:57.892
manage information, and receive data

00:05:57.892 --> 00:05:59.452
on how people interact with them,

00:05:59.852 --> 00:06:01.392
and they can build a business agent

00:06:01.392 --> 00:06:03.932
to answer customer questions and surface offerings.

00:06:03.932 --> 00:06:10.478
Gemini for health care, the Google AI blog details, unifies clinical data and automates

00:06:10.478 --> 00:06:15.638
workflows on Google Cloud, the offering targets administrative burnout by connecting records

00:06:15.638 --> 00:06:20.798
and streamlining processes, and early users can explore the new clinical capabilities in

00:06:20.798 --> 00:06:22.038
the Google Cloud console.

00:06:23.119 --> 00:06:27.799
Adobe Creative and Productivity tools now integrate directly with Google Apps and Gemini.

00:06:28.439 --> 00:06:33.079
Users can edit PDFs and drive and access Adobe AI features inside Gemini.

00:06:33.079 --> 00:06:40.032
so those creative tools sit inside every day Google Workflows. OpenAI Academy, the OpenAI blog

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:46.832
notes, expands free chat GPT workshops to caregivers in five U.S. cities. The hands-on sessions focus

00:06:46.832 --> 00:06:53.152
on practical everyday uses of AI, and registration is on the OpenAI site for people in the selected cities.

00:06:54.153 --> 00:07:00.773
Anthropic begins its initial public offering, or IPO, road show with a filed S1 registration statement

00:07:00.773 --> 00:07:06.213
on its site. Investor meetings are underway ahead of a potential listing and securities may

00:07:06.213 --> 00:07:12.151
not be sold until the registration statement becomes effective. From archive, actionable feedback

00:07:12.151 --> 00:07:17.931
uses a taxonomy of clinician editing behaviors plus filters so models can train on documentation

00:07:17.931 --> 00:07:23.371
edits without learning to hallucinate, improving alignment metrics while remaining faithful to the

00:07:23.371 --> 00:07:29.451
input context. Cell detects silent evidence loss in context compression even when the final answer

00:07:29.451 --> 00:07:32.591
or stays unchanged, comparing reader model preferences

00:07:32.591 --> 00:07:34.951
before and after compression without labels

00:07:34.951 --> 00:07:37.171
and identifying the evidence-removing edit

00:07:37.171 --> 00:07:39.151
in 83% of matched pairs.

00:07:39.911 --> 00:07:43.231
Deletion sensitivity varies by 55.7 points

00:07:43.231 --> 00:07:45.211
across seven open reasoning models

00:07:45.491 --> 00:07:48.471
when full history is stripped in multi-turn tool sessions,

00:07:48.931 --> 00:07:52.031
a stable model level property measurable with two runs.

00:07:52.731 --> 00:07:55.731
Medical claims each link to a version source text span

00:07:55.731 --> 00:07:58.711
in a new evidence traceable benchmark spanning guideline,

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:04.571
scenario, and real world levels, and 10 LLMs show that guideline recall does not

00:08:04.571 --> 00:08:06.871
guarantee patient-specific evidence use.

00:08:07.491 --> 00:08:12.311
One sequence is enough fingerprints 51 language models from a single fixed length integer

00:08:12.311 --> 00:08:19.131
sequence at 92.72% closed set accuracy, and adding a second and fourth answer raises that

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:24.391
to 96.06% and 97.12%.

00:08:24.391 --> 00:08:30.931
ESOBR releases an open, balanced 896 item corpus for misogyny detection in Brazilian Portuguese,

00:08:31.351 --> 00:08:39.691
with Fleiscappa of 0.788, where fine-tuned Bertambau reaches 0.833 macro F1, and classical

00:08:39.691 --> 00:08:41.891
baselines cluster around 0.66.

00:08:42.791 --> 00:08:48.011
First aid question answer work is the job of hands-on aid, which fine-tunes a 4-bit Gemma

00:08:48.011 --> 00:08:55.331
2 billion model on 5,550 pairs, and scores 2.51 out of 5 on medically reviewed references,

00:08:55.851 --> 00:09:01.531
with a retrieval augmented version producing first text in 6.86 seconds on a Pixel 7 Pro

00:09:01.531 --> 00:09:05.671
with no network. Transformers trained on synthetic context-free

00:09:05.671 --> 00:09:10.851
grammars with variable parse trees show stage-wise emergence of inside outside computation,

00:09:11.431 --> 00:09:16.571
with early layers handling local bi-gram information, and later layers refining predictions around

00:09:16.571 --> 00:09:19.211
on an abstract latent tree encoded in the middle layers.

00:09:20.231 --> 00:09:22.031
Representational atoms can be recovered

00:09:22.031 --> 00:09:24.751
by threshold activated sparse auto encoders

00:09:24.751 --> 00:09:27.531
with high fidelity and stability when conditions are met.

00:09:28.231 --> 00:09:30.691
And stable atoms show greater monosomanticity

00:09:30.691 --> 00:09:34.071
and compose across layers to match human conceptual structure.

